-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 40, 41 and 41.2: SICKNESS, PREGNANCY, and the
-- MEDICAL CERTIFICATE OUTSIDE CANADA.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- What the person must give the Commission (the certificate, the statement of pregnancy), what the Commission
-- may require of them (an examination) and at whose cost, which illness or pregnancy counts, and when the
-- waiting period may be waived. Judgments of the Commission (what time and place are reasonable; whether to
-- waive) are inputs and are never guessed.
-- Out of range: s 8(2)(a), 18(1)(b), 22, 28(7), 152.03(1), 152.04 and the medical certificate subsections of
-- ss 23.1 to 23.3 and 152.06 to 152.062 of the Act (pieces ei1, ei2 and ei5); reg 14(2), 14.01 (piece er1);
-- reg 76.421 (piece er4) reads reg 40(6)(b) differently for provincial benefits and is that piece's.

§ `Regulation 40 -- sickness`

-- (1) The information and evidence a claimant must give to prove inability to work because of illness, injury or
-- quarantine is a medical certificate, completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional, attesting
-- to the claimant's inability to work and stating the probable duration.
-- src:709 | 40 (1) The information and evidence to be provided to the Commission by a claimant in order to prove inability to work because of illness, injury or quarantine under paragraph 18(1)(b) or subsection 152.03(1) of the Act, is a medical certificate completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional attesting to the claimant’s inability to work and stating the probable duration of the illness, injury or quarantine.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 40(1) (src:709)
GIVEN `the certificate is completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate attests to the claimant's inability to work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states the probable duration of the illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 40(1) the medical certificate is the information and evidence required` IF
        `the certificate is completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional`
    AND `the certificate attests to the claimant's inability to work`
    AND `the certificate states the probable duration of the illness, injury or quarantine`

-- (2) "Notwithstanding that a certificate is provided", the Commission may require a claimant to undergo a
-- medical examination at such time and place as it may reasonably direct, to determine the nature of the
-- illness, injury or quarantine, the claimant's physical or mental condition, the probable duration of the
-- inability to work and any other circumstances relating to it. The certificate does not matter, so it is not an
-- input. The claimant is liable to the requirement if the Commission has directed the examination and the time
-- and place directed are reasonable (whether they are is a judgment, an input).
-- src:711 | (2) Notwithstanding that a certificate is provided by a claimant pursuant to subsection (1), the Commission may require a claimant to undergo a medical examination at such time and place as it may reasonably direct for the purpose of determining the nature of the illness, injury or quarantine, the physical or mental condition of the claimant, the probable duration of the inability to work and any other circumstances relating to that inability.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 40(2) (src:711)
GIVEN `the Commission has directed the claimant to undergo a medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time and place the Commission directs are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 40(2) the claimant may be required to undergo a medical examination` IF
        `the Commission has directed the claimant to undergo a medical examination`
    AND `the time and place the Commission directs are reasonable`

-- (3) The examination is at the Commission's expense, and the claimant who undergoes it is reimbursed for their
-- reasonable travel and other expenses: the reasonable part of what they spent. An examination that is not one
-- required under (2) is not covered by (3): NOTHING.
-- src:712 | (3) A medical examination referred to in subsection (2) shall be made at the expense of the Commission and a claimant who undergoes such an examination shall be reimbursed for their reasonable travel and other expenses.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 40(3) (src:712)
GIVEN `the examination is one the Commission required under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's travel and other expenses of the examination` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those expenses that is reasonable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 40(3) the amount the claimant is reimbursed for the examination` IS
    IF `the examination is one the Commission required under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST (min `the claimant's travel and other expenses of the examination` `the part of those expenses that is reasonable`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) For the purposes of ss 8(2)(a), 18(1)(b), 28(7) and 152.03(1) of the Act, an illness, injury or
-- quarantine is one "that renders a claimant incapable of performing the duties of their regular or usual
-- employment or of other suitable employment". It is read as: incapable of both (fork F11).
-- src:713 | (4) For the purposes of paragraphs 8(2)(a) and 18(1)(b) and subsections 28(7) and 152.03(1) of the Act, illness, injury or quarantine is any illness, injury or quarantine that renders a claimant incapable of performing the duties of their regular or usual employment or of other suitable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 40(4) (src:713)
GIVEN `the claimant has an illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it renders the claimant incapable of performing the duties of their regular or usual employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it renders the claimant incapable of performing the duties of other suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 40(4) illness, injury or quarantine` IF
        `the claimant has an illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND `it renders the claimant incapable of performing the duties of their regular or usual employment`
    AND `it renders the claimant incapable of performing the duties of other suitable employment`

-- (5) A pregnancy that is terminated within the first 19 weeks is an illness for the purposes of paragraph
-- 18(1)(b) and subsection 152.03(1) of the Act. Within the first 19 weeks is read as: the pregnancy had run 19
-- weeks or less when it ended (fork F12).
-- src:714 | (5) A pregnancy that is terminated within the first 19 weeks is an illness for the purposes of paragraph 18(1)(b) and subsection 152.03(1) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 40(5) (src:714)
GIVEN `the pregnancy was terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks the pregnancy had run when it was terminated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 40(5) a pregnancy terminated within the first 19 weeks is an illness` IF
        `the pregnancy was terminated`
    AND `the number of weeks the pregnancy had run when it was terminated` AT MOST 19

-- (6) The Commission may waive the waiting period if (a) the claimant qualifies by an interruption of earnings
-- described in reg 14(2) or 14.01, and (b) after the claimant ceased to work, allowances, payments or other
-- moneys are payable by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay. The text gives the
-- Commission the power; the rule answers whether the two conditions are met, and the Commission's decision to
-- exercise the power is left to the caller. Reg 76.421 (piece er4) reads (b) differently where provincial benefits
-- were paid.
-- src:715 | (6) The Commission may waive the waiting period in respect of the benefit period of a claimant if
-- src:716 | (a) the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in that benefit period by reason of an interruption of earnings as described in subsection 14(2) or section 14.01; and
-- src:717 | (b) after the claimant ceased to work, allowances, payments or other moneys are payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 40(6) (src:715-717)
GIVEN `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in that benefit period by reason of an interruption of earnings as described in subsection 14(2) or section 14.01` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the claimant ceased to work, allowances, payments or other moneys are payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 40(6) the conditions on which the Commission may waive the waiting period are met` IF
        `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits in that benefit period by reason of an interruption of earnings as described in subsection 14(2) or section 14.01`
    AND `after the claimant ceased to work, allowances, payments or other moneys are payable to the claimant by the claimant's employer or former employer as sick leave pay`

-- reg 40(1.1) [Repealed, SOR/2020-44, s. 1] (line 710); reg 40(7), (8), (9) [Repealed, SOR/2020-44, s. 1]
-- (lines 718 to 720); reg 40.1 [Repealed, SOR/2020-44, s. 3] (line 721).

§ `Regulation 41 -- pregnancy`

-- (1) The information and evidence to prove pregnancy and the expected date of confinement is (a) a statement
-- signed by the claimant attesting to her pregnancy and declaring her expected date of confinement; and (b)
-- information regarding the actual date of the child's birth, given to the Commission in person, by mail or by
-- telephone as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth. Paragraph (b) cannot be met before the birth, so
-- it is required only once the child has been born (fork F13). "As soon as reasonably possible" is a judgment
-- of fact on the claimant's side: an input.
-- src:726 | (b) information regarding the actual date of the birth of the child, provided by the claimant to the Commission in person, by mail or by telephone as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth of the child.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 41(1)(b) (src:726)
GIVEN `the child has been born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has given the Commission information regarding the actual date of the birth, in person, by mail or by telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she gave it as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 41(1)(b) the information regarding the actual date of the birth is given as required` IS
    IF `the child has been born`
    THEN `the claimant has given the Commission information regarding the actual date of the birth, in person, by mail or by telephone` AND `she gave it as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth`
    ELSE TRUE

-- src:724 | 41 (1) For the purposes of sections 22 and 152.04 of the Act, the information and evidence to be provided to the Commission by a claimant to prove pregnancy and the expected date of confinement is
-- src:725 | (a) a statement signed by the claimant attesting to her pregnancy and declaring her expected date of confinement; and
-- src:726 | (b) information regarding the actual date of the birth of the child, provided by the claimant to the Commission in person, by mail or by telephone as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth of the child.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 41(1) (src:724-726)
GIVEN `the claimant has signed a statement attesting to her pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement declares her expected date of confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child has been born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has given the Commission information regarding the actual date of the birth, in person, by mail or by telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she gave it as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 41(1) the information and evidence of pregnancy is given` IF
        `the claimant has signed a statement attesting to her pregnancy`
    AND `the statement declares her expected date of confinement`
    AND `reg 41(1)(b) the information regarding the actual date of the birth is given as required` `the child has been born` `the claimant has given the Commission information regarding the actual date of the birth, in person, by mail or by telephone` `she gave it as soon as is reasonably possible after the birth`

-- (2) For the purposes of paragraph 8(2)(a) of the Act, a pregnancy is any pregnancy that renders a claimant
-- incapable of performing the duties of her regular or usual employment or of other suitable employment: read as
-- incapable of both, as in 40(4) (fork F11).
-- src:727 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph 8(2)(a) of the Act, a pregnancy is any pregnancy that renders a claimant incapable of performing the duties of her regular or usual employment or of other suitable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 41(2) (src:727)
GIVEN `the claimant is pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pregnancy renders her incapable of performing the duties of her regular or usual employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pregnancy renders her incapable of performing the duties of other suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 41(2) pregnancy` IF
        `the claimant is pregnant`
    AND `the pregnancy renders her incapable of performing the duties of her regular or usual employment`
    AND `the pregnancy renders her incapable of performing the duties of other suitable employment`

-- reg 41.1 [Repealed, SOR/2017-226, s. 10] (line 728); reg 41.11 [Repealed, SOR/2017-226, s. 10] (line 729).

§ `Regulation 41.2 -- medical certificate outside Canada`

-- For the parental, compassionate care, critically ill child and critically ill adult benefits (the subsections
-- of the Act it names), the medical certificate may be issued by an individual authorized by the appropriate
-- governmental authority of a country other than Canada to perform the work of a medical doctor or nurse
-- practitioner, with professional qualifications substantially similar to those of one practising in Canada, if the
-- person the certificate refers to is in that country.
-- src:734 | 41.2 For the purposes of subsections 23.1(3), 23.2(2), 23.3(2), 152.06(2), 152.061(2) and 152.062(2) of the Act, the medical certificate referred to in subsections 23.1(2), 23.2(1), 23.3(1), 152.06(1), 152.061(1) or 152.062(1) of the Act may be issued by an individual authorized by the appropriate governmental authority of a country other than Canada to perform the work of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner and who has professional qualifications that are substantially similar to those of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner practising in Canada, if the person to whom the certificate refers is in that country.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 41.2 (src:734)
GIVEN `the individual is authorized by the appropriate governmental authority of a country other than Canada to perform the work of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has professional qualifications that are substantially similar to those of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner practising in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom the certificate refers is in that country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 41.2 the medical certificate issued outside Canada may be accepted` IF
        `the individual is authorized by the appropriate governmental authority of a country other than Canada to perform the work of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner`
    AND `the individual has professional qualifications that are substantially similar to those of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner practising in Canada`
    AND `the person to whom the certificate refers is in that country`

-- reg 41.3, 41.4 and 41.5 [Repealed, SOR/2017-226, s. 10] (lines 735 to 737).
